  "typical_application": "Clocked 8-bit register / output port that captures bus data on a rising clock edge and drives a 3-state bus.",
  "gotchas": [
    "GND = pin 10, VCC = pin 20",
    "CLK (pin 11) is rising-edge triggered: data sampled only on the LOW-to-HIGH transition (a flip-flop, not a transparent latch like the '373)",
    "OE (pin 1) is active-LOW and only controls the 3-state outputs; it does not affect stored data",
    "same interleaved D/Q layout as the '373; pin 11 is CLK here, LE on the '373"
